      "## The AI conversation is missing an important piece",
      "Every week, a new AI model claims to be smarter, faster, or cheaper. But one question often gets overlooked: what happens when you take the same model and give it a different environment in which to work?",
      "Ask a model to fix a bug or automate a business process, and its success depends on more than a good answer. It needs the right context, appropriate tools, a way to execute actions, and a method for checking whether those actions worked. That surrounding infrastructure, the harness, is the difference between a system that explains how to do something and one that can actually attempt it.",
      "## 1. What is an AI harness?",
      "An AI harness is the software and orchestration layer that surrounds a model and manages how it is used to perform a task. There is no single universal definition. In model evaluation, it can mean software that runs tests and scores outputs, as in [EleutherAI's lm-evaluation-harness](https://github.com/EleutherAI/lm-evaluation-harness). This article focuses on the agent harness: the infrastructure that manages instructions, tool calls, execution, context, and the interaction loop.",
