      "**Skills and memory.** [Skills](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/skills) are procedural knowledge, such as how to investigate a repository or follow a deployment workflow, loaded when relevant instead of included in every request. [Memory](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/features/memory) preserves selected facts across sessions. Memory helps the agent remember what it knows. Skills help it follow how to do something. Neither guarantees that the stored information is current or correct.",
      "**When it makes sense.** Hermes is worth evaluating for recurring research, development tasks, and scheduled jobs. It may be unnecessary when a direct model call would do. Hermes has [documented security controls](https://hermes-agent.nousresearch.com/docs/user-guide/security), but users still need to configure and evaluate them for their environment. The lesson is not that everyone should use Hermes, but that knowing what a framework adds helps you decide whether you need one.",
      "## 4. How to choose the right model for the task",
