      "For specialized benchmarks, [SWE-bench](https://www.swebench.com/) evaluates software engineering tasks drawn from real GitHub issues. [LiveCodeBench](https://livecodebench.github.io/) evaluates code generation, self-repair, and related skills on problems collected continuously from coding contests. [OSWorld](https://osworld-v1.xlang.ai/) evaluates agents on computer-use tasks in real operating-system environments. Their scores are not interchangeable; runs may use different harnesses. A benchmark should tell you which candidates are worth testing. It should not make the decision for you.",
